body: |-
  Performance (.paradigm/research/session-2026-11-24/performance-audit.md):
  - The cost a person feels is the Stop hook: 3.3 to 3.9 s on every code-touching turn in this repo. Most of it was one `find` from the project root, run twice, over about 80,000 entries (Warpline objects and Swift build trees the prune list did not know).
  - Fix (#108): one file list per run from `git ls-files`, with a pruned walk as the fallback. Portal check 2,483 ms to 220 ms on this checkout; doctor 2.8 s to 0.5 s in a scratch copy. Not yet confirmed on a real Stop.
  - Already fast and left alone: CLI start-up (about 60 ms), per-edit and per-prompt hooks, MCP tool handlers.
  - Corrected an earlier reviewer: decoding the embedded GUI bundle takes 0.44 ms and is not a hot path. The real problem is size and reach: the agent client imports two helpers from the daemon CLI, which drags the GUI bundle into six places in a global install.
  - Also found: two Paradigm MCP servers per session (plugin and .mcp.json); `paradigm_search` defaults to detailed output (65,000 characters for a two-word query against 948 concise).

  Symbol hygiene (symbol-hygiene-audit.md):
  - Five `.purpose` files failed YAML parsing and were silently dropped from the index (94 symbol entries). `paradigm lint` exited 1 on the framework's own repo.
  - `status` counts 232 phantom symbols scraped from prose, including `$HOME` as a flow.
  - `status` and `doctor` disagree on gates, files and isolated symbols; doctor's "1 lore file" is a checker bug (714 exist).
  - Fix (#106): the five files parse; 43 anchors, 11 line ranges, 2 file fields and 3 parents corrected; 26 duplicate definitions removed; AGENTS.md no longer links the wrong GitHub org.

  What review added:
  - On #108, framed as enforcement code: a broad ignore pattern could hide a new gate file from the git list with no signal, so an undeclared gate would pass where the old walk blocked; and the code scan and the file list covered different trees, giving a false block for a gate declared inside a submodule. The builder reproduced all four scenarios (16 of 23 new tests failed on the first version) before fixing. Also: the git timeout equalled the hook's own 30 s timeout, so a hang would have meant no enforcement at all.
  - On #106: quoting two prefixed signal keys was the wrong repair (they index double-prefixed; the prefix was dropped instead), and a rename had been applied to a spec row the spec itself says stands as history.
  - The builder on #106 found the audit understated one defect: prefixed keys inside a section block are double-prefixed in the index itself, in 27 files.

  Left open on purpose: two fail-open paths in the compliance check (a crashing portal check passes; a missing search tool reads as no matches), which need their own change because fixing them starts blocking; casing for 28 twin symbol pairs; 11 portal routes with no handler.

  Operational note: the Mac's disk reached 100% during these runs (test temp directories and worktree dependency folders); 3.8 GB of the session's own leftovers were cleared.
